# Agent worktrees hold whole copies of this repo, so `pnpm format` reaches into
# other in-flight branches and rewrites their files. Prettier reads .gitignore
# too, and this stays for anyone who runs it with --no-ignore-unknown elsewhere.
.claude

# `changeset version` rewrites these and formats them itself, resolving Prettier
# from the repo and reading `.prettierrc` but not this file. So listing them here
# does not keep them unformatted, and `pnpm format` reproduces exactly what the
# release writes. The entry is belt and braces, and `proseWrap: never` is why one
# release unwrapped every historical entry.
CHANGELOG.md

# How a changeset body wraps does not change how the released entry reads, so
# reflowing these only rewrites prose someone chose the shape of. Scoped to the
# entries: `config.json` stays formatted.
.changeset/*.md

# Local working notes, untracked. .gitignore keeps it out of git and Prettier
# reads that too, but the formatting exemption belongs here: this file is the
# reason `pnpm lint` stays green if CLAUDE.md is ever tracked, and someone
# removing the .gitignore line would otherwise turn the lint job red with
# nothing near the edit explaining why.
/CLAUDE.md

/AGENTS.md
.clinerules/
.cursor/
.opencode/
.windsurf/
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Editor state, matching eslint.config.js. Neither is tracked, and a lint gate
# that fails on a local IDE file is reporting on something that is not the repo.
.idea
.vscode
